# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template. `.env*` also matched `.env.example`, so it was never
# committed — while the README instructs `cp .env.example .env` as the REQUIRED
# first setup step. A fresh clone therefore could not follow its own instructions,
# and any env var documented there (e.g. REVALIDATE_SECRET) reached nobody.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Playwright
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# BMAD workspace — planning artifacts, story files, skills and resolver config.
# Local-only by decision (2026-08-13), when GreenLighthouse was separated from the
# shared C:\AL workspace it used to share with LogiSupp. CLAUDE.md still points at
# these paths; they simply live inside the repo folder now instead of one level up.
/_bmad-output/
/_bmad/
/.claude/

# EXCEPTION (2026-08-25): the UX design source IS versioned.
#
# Why: DESIGN.md named a machine-local Pencil `.pen` path as "source of truth for
# layout". The export step was skipped, so the canvas survived only as a
# content-addressed blob in a tool's cache, named by its hash and findable by no
# search. Five Epic 2 story records checked the named path, found nothing, and
# recorded "there is no mock" — and four surfaces were designed at dev-kickoff from
# prose while their frames sat one directory outside the repo. Recovering it into an
# untracked folder would have left the same failure one step less severe.
#
# Git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, so each level has
# to be re-included and then re-emptied in turn. Everything else under
# `_bmad-output/` (implementation artifacts, story files, the deferred ledger)
# stays local-only exactly as before.
!/_bmad-output/
/_bmad-output/*
!/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/
/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/*
!/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/ux-designs/
